<http://data.silknow.org/event/2354b483-c0ca-3e6e-a6f7-1c0ab4317736>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Boys' dress of magenta and black. It was worn by Theophilus Willway when he was about 6 years old and donated to the museum by his great neice and nephew, along with another of his dresses and a pair of shoes and a silk party dress of c.1895, worn by the donors' mother, Lucy Ainsworth (b.1884 - d. 1978)\nTheophilus went on to become a photographer, first training under Frieze-Green of Bristol. He never married."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/65d224db-ba21-3671-b1f1-353dc4b175ff> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Boys' dress of magenta and black. It was worn by Theophilus Willway when he was about 6 years old and donated to the museum by his great neice and nephew, along with another of his dresses and a pair of shoes and a silk party dress of c.1895, worn by the donors' mother, Lucy Ainsworth (b.1884 - d. 1978)\nTheophilus went on to become a photographer, first training under Frieze-Green of Bristol. He never married."@en .

